The Netherlands entered the World Cup having won all eight matches in [[2010 FIFA World Cup qualification – UEFA Group 9|their qualifying campaign]].<ref name="RSSSF_Qual"/> They were then drawn in [[2010 FIFA World Cup Group E|Group E]] for the World Cup, in which they were joined by [[Cameroon national football team|Cameroon]], [[Denmark national football team|Denmark]] and [[Japan national football team|Japan]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Group E: Cameroon, Denmark, Japan, Netherlands |last=Corrigan |first=James |work=[[The Independent]] |date=23 October 2011 |access-date=4 October 2021 |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/international/group-e-cameroon-denmark-japan-netherlands-1993992.html |archive-date=4 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211004200611/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/international/group-e-cameroon-denmark-japan-netherlands-1993992.html |url-status=live}}</ref> Their first match was against Denmark at [[FNB Stadium|Soccer City]], on 14 June 2010.<ref name="GuardianNetherlandsDenmark">{{Cite web |title=Holland 2–0 Denmark |last=Wilson |first=Paul |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=14 June 2010 |access-date=4 October 2021 |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2010/jun/14/holland-denmark-world-cup |archive-date=4 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211004200558/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2010/jun/14/holland-denmark-world-cup |url-status=live}}</ref> The Netherlands took the lead shortly after [[half-time]] when Denmark's [[Simon Poulsen]] cleared a [[Cross (association football)|cross]] from [[Robin van Persie]], but it struck the back of [[Daniel Agger]] and deflected in for an [[own goal]].<ref name="BBCNetherlandsDenmark">{{Cite web |title=Netherlands 2–0 Denmark |last=Stevenson |first=Jonathan |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=14 June 2010 |access-date=4 October 2021 |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_09/default.stm |archive-date=4 March 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120304150831/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_09/default.stm |url-status=live}}</ref> [[Dirk Kuyt]] added a second five minutes before the end to complete a 2–0 win, scoring on the rebound after [[Thomas Sørensen]], the Danish [[goalkeeper (association football)|goalkeeper]], had saved [[Eljero Elia]]'s shot on to the goalpost.<ref name="GuardianNetherlandsDenmark" /><ref name="BBCNetherlandsDenmark" /> The Netherlands faced Japan in their second game, on 19 June at the [[Moses Mabhida Stadium]] in [[Durban]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=World Cup 2010: Holland v Japan – as it happened |last=Burnton |first=Simon |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=19 June 2010 |access-date=4 October 2021 |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2010/jun/19/world-cup-2010-holland-japan |archive-date=4 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211004201732/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2010/jun/19/world-cup-2010-holland-japan |url-status=live}}</ref> As in the first game, they scored the opening goal shortly after half-time when [[Wesley Sneijder]] received the ball on the edge of the [[penalty area]], following an attempted clearance by Japan, and struck the ball into the goal.<ref>{{Cite web |title=World Cup 2010: Netherlands 1–0 Japan: Wesley Sneijder strike puts Dutch in commanding position in Group E |last=Coerts |first=Stefan |website=[[Goal (website)|Goal]] |date=19 June 2010 |access-date=4 October 2021 |url=https://www.goal.com/en-gb/news/2890/world-cup-2010/2010/06/19/1984616/world-cup-2010-netherlands-1-0-japan-wesley-sneijder-strike-puts- |archive-date=4 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211004201732/https://www.goal.com/en-gb/news/2890/world-cup-2010/2010/06/19/1984616/world-cup-2010-netherlands-1-0-japan-wesley-sneijder-strike-puts- |url-status=live}}</ref> The win, alongside Denmark's victory over Cameroon, meant that the Netherlands had qualified for the next round before playing their final group game.<ref name="GuardianTaylorNetherlandsJapan">{{Cite web |last=Taylor |first=Daniel |title=Holland 1–0 Japan |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=21 June 2010 |access-date=4 October 2021 |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2010/jun/21/holland-japan-world-cup-match-report |archive-date=4 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211004201734/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2010/jun/21/holland-japan-world-cup-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref> That game was against Cameroon, on 24 June at [[Cape Town Stadium]]. Van Persie gave them the lead on 36 minutes,<ref>{{Cite web |title=Cameroon vs Netherlands. FIFA World Cup Group E |publisher=[[Sky Sports]] |date=24 June 2010 |access-date=4 October 2021 |url=https://www.skysports.com/football/cameroon-vs-netherlands/teams/211312 |archive-date=4 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211004204744/https://www.skysports.com/football/cameroon-vs-netherlands/teams/211312 |url-status=live}}</ref> before [[Samuel Eto'o]] equalised with a [[Penalty kick (association football)|penalty]] after [[Rafael van der Vaart]] was penalised for a [[Glossary of association football terms#H|handball]] in the penalty area. Klaas Jan Huntelaar scored a late goal, however, to seal a 2–1 win and first place in the group.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Cameroon 1–2 Netherlands |last=Bevan |first=Chris |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=24 June 2010 |access-date=4 October 2021 |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_44/default.stm |archive-date=14 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211014075357/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_44/default.stm |url-status=live}}</ref>

The Netherlands' round-of-16 game was against [[Slovakia national football team|Slovakia]], who had beaten Italy in their final group game, at the Moses Mabhida Stadium on 28 June. [[Arjen Robben]] started his first game of the tournament after recovering from an injury, and he gave the Netherlands the lead in the 18th minute when he received a long pass upfield by Sneijder and scored with a low shot past goalkeeper [[Ján Mucha]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=World Cup 2010: Arjen Robben steers Holland past limp Slovakia |last=Taylor |first=Daniel |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=28 June 2010 |access-date=6 October 2021 |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2010/jun/28/holland-slovakia-world-cup-2010-match-report |archive-date=6 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211006102600/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2010/jun/28/holland-slovakia-world-cup-2010-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref> Sneijder then added a second in the 84th minute before Slovakia scored a penalty in the final minute of [[injury time]], giving a final score of 2–1 to the Netherlands.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Netherlands 2–1 Slovakia |last=Dawkes |first=Phil |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=28 June 2010 |access-date=6 October 2021 |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_53/default.stm |archive-date=14 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211014075359/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_53/default.stm |url-status=live}}</ref> In the quarter-final, the Netherlands faced five-times world champions [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]], on 2 July at the [[Nelson Mandela Bay Stadium]] in [[Port Elizabeth]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Brazil, a World Cup Favorite, Is Sent Home |last=Longman |first=Jeré |work=[[The New York Times]] |url-access=registration |date=2 July 2010 |access-date=6 October 2021 |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2010/07/03/sports/soccer/03brazilgame.html |archive-date=6 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211006102600/https://www.nytimes.com/2010/07/03/sports/soccer/03brazilgame.html |url-status=live}}</ref> Brazil took the lead in the 10th minute, when [[Robinho]] latched on to a deep pass from [[Felipe Melo]] and scored.<ref name="BBCNedBra">{{cite news |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_57/default.stm |title=Netherlands 2–1 Brazil |last=Bevan |first=Chris |date=2 July 2010 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |access-date=2 July 2010 |archive-date=1 July 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100701190212/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_57/default.stm |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="FoxNedBra">{{cite news |url=http://www.foxsports.com.au/story/0,8659,27355567-5019291,00.html |title=The Netherlands upset Brazil 2–1 in FIFA World Cup quarter-final, South Africa |last=MacKinnon |first=Angus |date=3 July 2010 |publisher=[[Fox Sports (Australia)|Fox Sports]]|access-date=2 July 2010|archive-date=14 October 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211014075404/https://www.foxsports.com.au/akam/11/pixel_6215eccf|url-status=live}}</ref> Goalkeeper [[Maarten Stekelenburg]] had to make several saves to prevent Brazil extending their lead. The Netherlands equalised eight minutes after half-time, the goal being initially recorded as an own goal by Melo but later credited to Sneijder.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/newsid=1266860/index.html |title=Sneijder credited with first goal in Dutch quarter-final victory |date=3 July 2010 |publisher=[[FIFA]] |access-date=3 July 2010 |archive-date=16 February 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100216115834/http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/newsid=1266860/index.html |url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/2010-07-03/sneijder-moves-into-tie-for-goal-scoring-lead-after-fifa-changes-credit.html |title=Sneijder Moves Into Tie for Goal-Scoring Lead After FIFA Changes Credit |last=Bensch |first=Bob |date=3 July 2010 |publisher=[[Bloomberg L.P.]] |access-date=9 July 2010 |archive-date=11 September 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110911035816/http://www.bloomberg.com/news/2010-07-03/sneijder-moves-into-tie-for-goal-scoring-lead-after-fifa-changes-credit.html |url-status=live}}</ref> The Netherlands then took the lead from a Robben corner kick in the 68th minute, Sneijder heading the ball in after a flick-on from Kuyt. Melo was [[Penalty card#Red card|sent off]] for a stamp on Robben, and the Netherlands went on to complete a 2–1 win.<ref name="BBCNedBra"/> Their semi-final was against [[Uruguay national football team|Uruguay]] at Cape Town Stadium on 6 July.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Form and head-to-head stats – Uruguay vs Netherlands |publisher=[[Sky Sports]] |date=6 July 2010 |access-date=6 October 2021 |url=https://www.skysports.com/football/uruguay-vs-netherlands/stats/220750 |archive-date=6 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211006110801/https://www.skysports.com/football/uruguay-vs-netherlands/stats/220750 |url-status=live}}</ref> [[Giovanni van Bronckhorst]] gave the Netherlands the lead on 18 minutes with a shot which deflected in off the goalpost, before [[Diego Forlán]] equalised from long-range for Uruguay shortly before half-time.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Netherlands beat Uruguay 3–2 to secure spot in final |publisher=[[France 24]] |date=6 July 2010 |agency=[[Agence France-Presse]] |access-date=6 October 2021 |url=https://www.france24.com/en/20100607-netherlands-beats-uruguay-reach-world-cup-final-semifinal-south-africa-football-soccer |archive-date=6 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211006113650/https://www.france24.com/en/20100607-netherlands-beats-uruguay-reach-world-cup-final-semifinal-south-africa-football-soccer |url-status=live}}</ref> The Netherlands retook the lead on 70 minutes when Sneijder scored with a shot which deflected off [[Maxi Pereira]], a Uruguayan [[Defender (association football)|defender]].<ref name="GuardianNetherlandsUruguayReport">{{Cite web |last=McCarra |first=Kevin |title=World Cup 2010: Holland hold nerve to beat Uruguay and head for final |author-link=Kevin McCarra |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=6 July 2010 |access-date=6 October 2021 |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2010/jul/06/holland-uruguay-world-cup-2010-semi-final |archive-date=6 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211006112150/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2010/jul/06/holland-uruguay-world-cup-2010-semi-final |url-status=live}}</ref> Uruguay's players protested that van Persie had been interfering with play in an [[offside (association football)|offside]] position, but the goal stood.<ref>{{Cite web |title=World Cup 2010: Uruguay v Holland – as it happened |last=Doyle |first=Paul |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=6 July 2010 |access-date=6 October 2021 |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2010/jul/06/world-cup-2010-holland-uruguay-live |archive-date=6 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211006112148/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2010/jul/06/world-cup-2010-holland-uruguay-live |url-status=live}}</ref> Robben extended their lead with a [[Header (association football)|header]] shortly afterwards, before Pereira scored during injury time to give a final score of 3–2 to the Netherlands.<ref name="GuardianNetherlandsUruguayReport"/>

